----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Design inspiration acknowledgements
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
This tool is a pure-stdlib, no-SDK Python static checker for Dart/Flutter.
It was designed independently, but its design was *conceptually* informed
by the following open-source projects. No source code from these projects
was copied; only ideas (generated-file exclusion, unused-dependency
detection, severity grading) were adopted. Their licenses are respected
and credited here in the spirit of open-source citizenship.

  - dart-re-analyzer (Rust, Apache-2.0)
      https://github.com/evaisse/dart-re-analyzer
      -> severity grading + exclude generated files (*.g.dart, etc.)

  - pedant (Dart, custom_lint)
      https://github.com/ivangalkindeveloper/pedant
      -> unused-import detection / relative-import conversion concepts.

  - flutter_analyzer_script (Python)
      https://github.com/radyhaggag/flutter_analyzer_script
      -> unused dependency detection (declared but never imported).

  - refactoroscope / code_analyzer (Python, multi-language)
      https://github.com/moinsen-dev/code_analyzer
      -> "declaration vs reference" unused detection approach.

  - Dart Code Linter / lint / dart-lint
      https://github.com/nestorsgarzonc/dart-code-linter
      https://github.com/hacker1024/dart-lint
      -> lint rule taxonomy reference.
